---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Support - ScoreSpace"
  description="Help for ScoreSpace's games for iMessage: getting started, common questions, and how to contact us."
  heading="Support"
  subtitle="Help for our games for iMessage."
>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:support@scorespace.net">support@scorespace.net</a> and we'll get
        back to you, usually within five business days. It helps if you tell us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Which game, and what you were doing when it went wrong.</li>
        <li>Your iPhone or iPad model and iOS version (Settings, then General, then About).</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if you have one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <p>
        Our games run inside Messages. There's no separate app to open, and nothing appears on
        your Home Screen. That's normal.
      </p>
      <p>To start a game:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open a conversation in Messages.</li>
        <li>Tap the + to the left of the text field.</li>
        <li>
          Scroll to the end of the app row and tap More, then pick the game. Since iOS 17, apps
          you haven't used recently aren't in the first row.
        </li>
        <li>Pick a mode and send an invitation into the chat. Your friend taps the card to join.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>

      <h3>I can't find the game in Messages.</h3>
      <p>
        Tap + in a conversation, then More at the end of the app row. If it still isn't listed,
        tap Edit at the bottom of that list and make sure the game is switched on.
      </p>

      <h3>The game's icon is blank in the app drawer.</h3>
      <p>
        This is an iOS caching quirk rather than a problem with the game. Deleting the game and
        reinstalling it usually clears it, and restarting your iPhone can help too.
      </p>

      <h3>My friend can't see my invitation.</h3>
      <p>
        Both of you need the game installed. Ask them to install it, then send the invitation
        again. The original card won't start working retroactively.
      </p>

      <h3>The game says the invitation is closed or expired.</h3>
      <p>
        That happens when the game has already started with someone else, or when both of you
        sent an invitation at the same moment and one had to give way. Send a new one.
      </p>

      <h3>My game won't sync between phones.</h3>
      <p>
        Check that both devices have a working internet connection, because the games need one
        to share a board. If a game seems stuck, close the panel and tap the card in the
        conversation again to pick it back up.
      </p>

      <h3>I lost my progress after reinstalling.</h3>
      <p>
        Your profile, settings and stats are stored on your device, so deleting the game deletes
        them. There's no account to restore from.
      </p>

      <h3>Do any of the games involve real money?</h3>
      <p>
        No. Chips in our card games are a play currency with no monetary value. They can't be
        bought, sold, transferred or redeemed, no real money is wagered at any point, and there
        are no in-app purchases.
      </p>

      <h3>Is there an Android version?</h3>
      <p>
        No. These games are built on iMessage and only run on iPhone and iPad.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our privacy policy: <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}privacy/`}>scorespace.net/privacy</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy questions and data deletion requests:
        <a href="mailto:privacy@scorespace.net">privacy@scorespace.net</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Requirements</h2>
      <p>iPhone or iPad running iOS 16.4 or later, with Messages.</p>

      <p class="legal-footer-note">
        See also our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}terms/`}>Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
